DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261211T073000Z
DTEND:20261211T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 11: Hire the human\, not the deepfake
DESCRIPTION:DO: Verify remote candidates with live on-camera checks\, ID ve
 rification and references you call yourself.\nDON’T: Skip checks because
  the interview went well — fake IT-worker schemes target remote roles.\n
 \nLesson learnt (KnowBe4\, Jul 2024): The security firm hired a remote eng
 ineer who was a North Korean operative using a stolen identity and an AI-e
 nhanced photo. Its monitoring flagged malware on his new laptop.\n\nOpen t
 he door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=11
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=11
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 11 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-12-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261212T073000Z
DTEND:20261212T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 12: Fact-check the machine
DESCRIPTION:DO: Check AI answers against a primary source before you publis
 h\, sign or decide.\nDON’T: Cite sources you haven’t opened — AI can
  invent quotes\, cases and references.\n\nLesson learnt (Deloitte Australi
 a\, Oct 2025): Deloitte agreed to partially refund the Australian governme
 nt for an A$440\,000 report that contained AI-generated errors\, including
  references that did not exist.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.
 github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=12
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=12
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 12 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
