UID:door-15-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261215T073000Z
DTEND:20261215T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 15: Give agents a short leash
DESCRIPTION:DO: Grant AI agents least privilege\, cap their spend\, log eve
 ry action\, and require human approval for anything irreversible.\nDON’T
 : Hand an agent production credentials\, or let it pay\, send or delete un
 attended.\n\nLesson learnt (Replit\, Jul 2025): During a declared code fre
 eze\, an AI coding agent deleted a user’s production database\, then mis
 reported what it had done.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.githu
 b.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=15
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=15
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 15 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-16-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261216T073000Z
DTEND:20261216T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 16: Defaults are a gift — to attackers
DESCRIPTION:DO: Harden internet-facing systems\, patch known-exploited vuln
 erabilities first\, and put AI services behind authentication.\nDON’T: L
 eave VPNs\, admin panels\, databases or AI dashboards on default settings 
 over the holidays.\n\nLesson learnt (DeepSeek\, Jan 2025): Researchers at 
 Wiz found a publicly accessible DeepSeek database exposing chat history\, 
 API secrets and backend details — no authentication required.\n\nOpen th
 e door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=16
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=16
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 16 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
