UID:door-17-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261217T073000Z
DTEND:20261217T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 17: Never trust the output
DESCRIPTION:DO: Validate and encode model output before it reaches a browse
 r\, shell or database — and fail closed on errors.\nDON’T: Pipe LLM ou
 tput into eval()\, SQL or innerHTML\, or skip a check when a service times
  out.\n\nLesson learnt (Vanna.AI\, Jun 2024): A prompt-injection flaw (CVE
 -2024-5565) let attackers run code\, because the library executed chart co
 de the model had written.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github
 .io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=17
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=17
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 17 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-18-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261218T073000Z
DTEND:20261218T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 18: Urgency is not identity
DESCRIPTION:DO: Verify callers through a fixed process before any password\
 , MFA or account change.\nDON’T: Reset MFA because a caller sounds right
  — voices can be cloned and urgency can be faked.\n\nLesson learnt (Mark
 s & Spencer\, Apr 2025): Attackers got in through social engineering invol
 ving a third party. M&S paused online orders for weeks and estimated a £3
 00 million hit to profit.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github
 .io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=18
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=18
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 18 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
