UID:door-22-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261222T073000Z
DTEND:20261222T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 22: Know what you ship
DESCRIPTION:DO: Pin dependencies and CI actions to full commit SHAs\, keep 
 an SBOM\, and verify signatures.\nDON’T: Install a package an AI assista
 nt suggests without checking it’s real — or load untrusted model files
 .\n\nLesson learnt (tj-actions/changed-files\, Mar 2025): Attackers re-poi
 nted the version tags of a popular GitHub Action to malicious code that du
 mped CI secrets into build logs (CVE-2025-30066).\n\nOpen the door: https:
 //aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=22
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=22
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 22 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-23-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261223T073000Z
DTEND:20261223T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 23: Read the AI small print
DESCRIPTION:DO: Ask every vendor: is our data used for training\, where is 
 it stored\, and who are the sub-processors?\nDON’T: Approve tools on cli
 ck-through terms without a security and privacy review.\n\nLesson learnt (
 MOVEit\, May 2023): A zero-day in a widely used file-transfer product let 
 the Cl0p gang steal data from thousands of organisations — many hit thro
 ugh their suppliers.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-by-design.github.io/C
 yberAIAdvent2026/?day=23
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=23
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 23 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-24-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261224T073000Z
DTEND:20261224T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 24: Ready when the office is empty
DESCRIPTION:DO: Staff an on-call rota\, route alerts to a human\, and keep 
 the incident plan and contacts offline.\nDON’T: Trust backups you’ve n
 ever restored — follow 3-2-1 and test a restore before the break.\n\nLes
 son learnt (British Library\, Oct 2023): Rhysida ransomware crippled servi
 ces for months. The library’s own lessons-learned report pointed to remo
 te access without MFA and legacy systems.\n\nOpen the door: https://aware-
 by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=24
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=24
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Door 24 is open
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:door-25-full-2026@cyber-advent-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T163445Z
DTSTART:20261225T073000Z
DTEND:20261225T073500Z
SUMMARY:Door 25: Talk AI with your kids
DESCRIPTION:DO: Explain that chatbots can be wrong and aren’t friends\, a
 nd set up age-appropriate controls together.\nDON’T: Let children share 
 their full name\, school\, photos or location with chatbots or strangers.\
 n\nLesson learnt (Italy’s Garante fines OpenAI\, Dec 2024): Italy’s da
 ta-protection authority fined OpenAI €15 million\, citing among other is
 sues the lack of adequate age verification for ChatGPT.\n\nOpen the door: 
 https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=25
URL:https://aware-by-design.github.io/CyberAIAdvent2026/?day=25
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
